        ":question/problem": "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z)$ a potential function?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z))\\,k \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,k \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,k.\n$$"
